en Republican Brandon Herrera and Democrat Katy Padilla Stout has settled into a genuinely competitive race. The district's Republican lean of seven points gives Herrera a structural advantage, but a favorable midterm environment for Democrats and the circumstances of the vacancy have kept Democrats within striking distance. The only recent poll, conducted in early October, showed the candidates tied at 46 percent.\n\nHerrera has a clear financial edge, raising about $3.1 million to Stout's $1.1 million, and holds Donald Trump's endorsement, though editorial boards and national commentators have criticized his candidacy. Most rating outlets call the race Lean Republican, while several see a toss-up, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a four-in-ten chance. An independent candidate, Ben Mendoza, adds a layer of uncertainty to the margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3496, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2679, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3125, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3009, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2961, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3821, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2984, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3321, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2493, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2959, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.266, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2185, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2336, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3266, "margi